faqs.answer:
Yes. Pass the axes handle returned by `subplot` or `gca` as the first argument.

```matlab
ax = subplot(2, 1, 1);
subtitle(ax, 'Top panel details');
```

Yes. `subtitle` returns a text handle, so you can update it with `set`.

```matlab
h = subtitle('Initial');
set(h, 'String', 'Updated', 'FontSize', 12);
```
